{"version":1,"slug":"Others__General_Awareness_-_General_Studies_-_Super_Practice_-_SSC_SUPER_PRACTICE_41984_(20Q)","path":"Others/General Awareness - General Studies - Super Practice - SSC SUPER PRACTICE 41984 (20Q).html","title":"devgagan","provider":"Others","category":"General Awareness - General Studies - Super Practice - SSC SUPER PRACTICE 41984 (20Q).html","durationMinutes":60,"totalQuestions":20,"sectionsLocked":false,"sections":null,"questions":[{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>What is the approximate area of a circular path of uniform width of 2.5 m surrounding a circular park with a diameter of 150 m?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>150 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2360; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2323;&#2352; 2.5 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2346;&#2341; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">1200 sq. m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1200 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1000 sq. m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1000 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1500 sq. m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1500 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">900 sq. m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">900 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Radius of park (r) = 150/2 = 75 m</p><p>Combined radius (R) = Radius of park + width of path = 75 + 2.5 = 77.5</p><p>Area of width = &#960; (R<sup>2</sup>  -  r<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>= (22/7) (77.5<sup>2</sup>  -  75<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>= (22/7) (152.5) (2.5)</p><p>= 1198.21 sq. m</p><p>= 1200 sq. m</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The sides of a triangular field are 39 m, 80 m, and 89 m. The cost of leveling the field at Rs.4.2 per sq. m is:</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2376;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; 39 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;, 80 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2324;&#2352; 89 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2350;&#2376;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2379; &#2360;&#2350;&#2340;&#2354; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; 4.2 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;:</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Rs.7225</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;.7225</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs.6552</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;.6552</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs.8221</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;.8221</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rs.9252</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2369;.9252</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>The given sides of the triangle are Pythagorean triplets.</p><p>Therefore,</p><p>Area of triangle = (1/2) x base x height</p><p>= (1/2) x 39 x 80 = 1560 m<sup>2</sup></p><p>Cost of levelling the field = 1560 x 4.2 = Rs.6552</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The area of a right-angled triangle is 60 sq. cm. If one of the sides forming the right angle is 15 cm, what is the length of the other side forming the right angle?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 60 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2360;&#2350;&#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; 15 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2360;&#2350;&#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">8 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">8 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">16 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">16 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">4 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">4 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">10 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">10 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>In the right-angled triangle, out of two sides that are containing the right angle, one works as the base and the other works as the height.</p><p>Area = (1/2) x Base x height</p><p>60 = (1/2) x 15 x height</p><p>Height = 120/15 = 8 cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Find the area of the isosceles triangle whose semi-perimeter is 16 cm, and each equal side is 10 cm.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2313;&#2360; &#2360;&#2350;&#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2367;&#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2369; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;-&#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; 16 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; 10 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">88 sq. cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">88 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">64 sq. cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">64 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">48 sq. cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">48 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">60 sq. cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">60 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Semi-perimeter = 16 cm</p><p>(10 + 10 + third side) = 32 cm</p><p>Third side = 12 cm</p><p><img width=192 height=28 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27578/image001.png\"></p><p><img width=143 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27578/image002.png\"></p><p><img width=103 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27578/image003.png\"></p><p><img width=105 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27578/image004.png\"></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The area of an equilateral triangle is <img width=59 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27578/image005.png\"> sq. cm. Find the circumference (correct to one decimal place) of a circle whose radius is equal to the side of this triangle.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2369; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; <img width=59 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27578/image005.png\"> &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2343;&#2367; (&#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344; &#2340;&#2325; &#2360;&#2361;&#2368;) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2311;&#2360; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">380.2 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">380.2 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">383.4 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">383.4 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">381.9 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">381.9 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">385.1 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">385.1 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p><img width=243 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27578/image006.png\"></p><p><img width=141 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27578/image007.png\"></p><p><img width=91 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27578/image008.png\"></p><p><img width=84 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27578/image009.png\"></p><p><img width=37 height=19 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27578/image010.png\"></p><p><img width=351 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27578/image011.png\"></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The radius of a circle is 25 cm. The base of a triangle is equal to the radius of this circle and the height of the triangle is 40% more than its base. Find the area of the triangle.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 25 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2319;&#2325; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2311;&#2360; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2305;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; 40% &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">437.5 sq. cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">437.5 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">410.2 sq. cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">410.2 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">522.5 sq. cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">522.5 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">501.2 sq. cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">501.2 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Base of triangle = 25 cm</p><p>Height of triangle = 25 x 140/100 = 35 cm</p><p>Area of the triangle = (1/2) x base x height</p><p>= (1/2) x 25 x 35</p><p>= 437.5 sq. cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The perimeter of a triangle is 10 times the circumference of a circle. If the radius of the circle is 7/11 cm, and the sides of triangle are 10 cm, 15 cm, and X cm, find the value of X.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2343;&#2367; &#2325;&#2366; 10 &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 7/11 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2324;&#2352; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; 10 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;, 15 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; X &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; X &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">12 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">12 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">22 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">22 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">20 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">20 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">15 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">15 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>10 x circumference of circle = Perimeter of triangle</p><p>10 x 2 x (22/7) x (7/11) = 10 + 15 + X</p><p>40 = 25 + X</p><p>X = 15 cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The difference between the circumferences of two circles is 30.8 cm. If the radii of the circles are 11.5 cm and Y cm, find the value of Y.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2343;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; 30.8 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; 11.5 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; Y &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; Y &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">6.6 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">6.6 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">4.9 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">4.9 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">2.8 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2.8 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">7.2 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">7.2 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Difference between circumferences = 30.8</p><p>2 x (22/7) x (11.5  -  Y) = 30.8</p><p>11.5  -  Y = 4.9</p><p>Y = 6.6 cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The sides of a triangle are 12, 14, and 9. The radius of a circle is equal to the perimeter of this triangle. Find the circumference of this circle.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; 12, 14 &#2324;&#2352; 9 &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2311;&#2360; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2343;&#2367; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2343;&#2367; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">110 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">110 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">220 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">220 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">180 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">180 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">260 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">260 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Perimeter = 12 + 14 + 9 = 35 cm</p><p>Radius of circle = 35 cm</p><p>Circumference of circle = 2 &#960; r = 2 x (22/7) x 35 = 220 cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The inner circumference of a circular track is 121/7 cm. Find the diameter of the outer circle of the track if the track is 10 cm wide.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2376;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2343;&#2367; 121/7 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2376;&#2325; 10 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2376;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2352;&#2368; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2360; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">25.5 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">25.5 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">24 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">24 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">25 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">25 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">24.5 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">24.5 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Inner circumference = 121/7</p><p>2&#960;r = 121/7</p><p>2 x (22/7) x r = 121/7</p><p>r = 11/4 = 2.75 cm</p><p>Outer radius of track = 2.75 + 10 = 12.75 cm</p><p>Diameter of outer circle of track = 12.75 x 2 = 25.5 cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Find the area of a triangle whose altitude and base are 17 cm and 10 cm, respectively.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2324;&#2352; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 17 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; 10 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">102 sq. cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">102 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">68 sq. cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">68 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">85 sq. cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">85 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">91 sq. cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">91 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Area of triangle = (1/2) x base x altitude</p><p>= (1/2) x 10 x 17</p><p>= 85 sq. cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The ratio between the radius of a circle and the side of an equilateral triangle is 9: 4 and the circumference of the circle is 198/7 cm. Find the perimeter of triangle.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2350;&#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2369; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 9:4 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2343;&#2367; 198/7 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">6 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">6 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">4 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">4 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">12 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">12 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">9 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">9 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Let the radius of the circle be 9X and side of the triangle be 4X.</p><p>Circumference of the circle = 198/7</p><p>2 x &#960; x (9X) = 198/7</p><p>2 x (22/7) x (9X) = 198/7</p><p>X = 1/2</p><p>Therefore, the side of the triangle be 4 x (1/2) = 2 cm</p><p>Perimeter of triangle = 2 + 2 + 2 = 6 cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The perimeter of a triangle is 24 and one side of the triangle is 11 cm. If the area of the triangle is 4&radic;21 sq. cm, find the other two sides of the triangle (in cm).</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; 24 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; 11 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 4&radic;21 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2309;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351; &#2342;&#2379; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; (&#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">6 and 7</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">6 &#2324;&#2352; 7</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">5 and 8</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">5 &#2324;&#2352; 8</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">4 and 9</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">4 &#2324;&#2352; 9</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">10 and 3</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">10 &#2324;&#2352; 3</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Let the second side of the triangle be X.</p><p>Then,</p><p>11 + X + third side = 24</p><p>Third side = 13 - X</p><p>Semi-perimeter = 24/2 = 12</p><p>Given,</p><p>Area = 4&radic;21</p><p><img width=273 height=28 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27578/image012.png\"></p><p><img width=188 height=23 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27578/image013.png\"></p><p><img width=148 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27578/image014.png\"></p><p><img width=116 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27578/image015.png\"></p><p><img width=112 height=23 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27578/image016.png\"></p><p><img width=63 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27578/image017.png\"></p><p><img width=185 height=19 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27578/image018.png\"></p><p><img width=188 height=19 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27578/image019.png\"></p><p><img width=212 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27578/image020.png\"></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The perimeter of an isosceles triangle is 151 cm. If the base is 43 cm, find the length of the equal sides.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2367;&#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2369; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; 151 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; 43 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">54 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">54 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">52 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">52 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">60 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">60 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">58 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">58 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Let the length of the equal sides be X cm.</p><p>Perimeter = 151</p><p>43 + X + X = 151</p><p>2X = 108</p><p>X = 54 cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>If the perimeter of a semicircle is 81 cm, find the diameter of the semicircle.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;&#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; 81 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;&#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2360; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">30.5 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">30.5 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">32.5 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">32.5 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">31.5 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">31.5 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">33.5 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">33.5 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Perimeter of semicircle = 81 cm</p><p><img width=73 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27578/image021.png\"></p><p><img width=79 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27578/image022.png\"></p><p><img width=99 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27578/image023.png\"></p><p><img width=65 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27578/image024.png\"></p><p><img width=45 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27578/image025.png\"></p><p><img width=280 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27578/image026.png\"></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The area of the circular park is 18634 m<sup>2</sup>. The path around this circular park has width 7 m. Find the area of circular path thus formed?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 18634 m<sup>2</sup> &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2311;&#2352;&#2381;&#2342; &#2327;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2342; &#2348;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2341; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; 7 m &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2348;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2346;&#2341; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">2300 m<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2300 m<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">3542 m<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3542 m<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">3267 m<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3267 m<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">4000 m<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">4000 m<sup>2</sup></span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Area of circular park = 18364 m<sup>2</sup></p><p>Area of circle = &#960;r<sup>2</sup></p><p>Therefore, &#960;r<sup>2</sup> = 18634</p><p><img width=99 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15683/image003.png\"></p><p><img width=101 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15683/image004.png\"></p><p><img width=104 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15683/image005.png\"></p><p>r = 11 X 7 = 77 m</p><p>Area of circular path = &#960;[(r+7)<sup>2</sup>  -  r<sup>2</sup>)]</p><p>= &#960;[(77+7)<sup>2</sup>  -  77<sup>2</sup>)]</p><p>= &#960;(84<sup>2</sup>  -  77<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>= &#960;(7056  -  5929)</p><p>= (22 X 1127)/7 = 161 X 22 = 3542 m<sup>2</sup></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The circumference of a circle is 264 cm. If the radius of the circle is equal to the side of the square, then find the perimeter of the square. </p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2343;&#2367; 264 cm &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;, &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">168 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">168 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">140 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">140 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">196 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">196 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">112 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">112 cm</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>The circumference of a circle = 2 &#960; r</p><p>264 = 2 * 22/7 * r</p><p>=> r = 264 * 7/ (2 * 22)</p><p>=> r = 42 cm</p><p>The perimeter of the square = 4 * Side</p><p>= 4 * 42 = 168 cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Diameter of a circle is equal to the diagonal of a square and sum of area of circle and that of square is 252 cm<sup>2</sup>, then what is the length of side of square? (Take &#960; = 22/7)</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2360; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; 252 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2375; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2350;&#2381;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;? (&#960; = 22/7 &#2354;&#2375;&#2306;)</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">7/&radic;2 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">7/&radic;2 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">7&radic;2 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">7&radic;2 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">14&radic;2 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">14&radic;2 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">14 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">14 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Let radius of circle be 'r' cm.</p><p>Let side of square be 'a' cm.</p><p>Now,</p><p>2r = a&radic;2</p><p><b>r = a/&radic;2 ....... (1)</b></p><p>Area of circle + Area of square = 252</p><p>&#960;r<sup>2</sup> + a<sup>2</sup> = 252</p><p>From equation (1):</p><p>&#960; * (a/&radic;2)<sup>2</sup> + a<sup>2</sup> = 252</p><p>a<sup>2</sup> [&#960;/2 + 1] = 252</p><p>a<sup>2</sup> [(11/7) + 1] = 252</p><p>a<sup>2</sup> (18/7) = 252</p><p>a<sup>2</sup> = 98</p><p>a = 7&radic;2</p><p>Length of side of square = 7&radic;2 cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Area of a circular garden is 55.44 m<sup>2</sup>. Sunil walks along the periphery of the park and completes ten rounds. What distance did Sunil covered while walking?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2348;&#2327;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 55.44 m<sup>2</sup> &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2360;&#2369;&#2344;&#2368;&#2354; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2343;&#2367; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2342;&#2367;&#2358; &#2330;&#2354;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2342;&#2360; &#2330;&#2325;&#2381;&#2325;&#2352; &#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2330;&#2354;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2369;&#2319; &#2360;&#2369;&#2344;&#2368;&#2354; &#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2368;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">264m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">264m</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">254m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">254m</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">234m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">234m</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">244m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">244m</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Area of a circle=<img width=99 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20757/image009.png\"></p><p>Radius=r=<img width=139 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20757/image010.png\"></p><p>Peripheral distance covered by Sunil in one round = 2&#960;R = (2  X  22  X  4.20)/7 = 26.40m</p><p>Distance covered in 10 rounds = 10  X  26.40 = 264m</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>A semi - circular cardboard of radius 3.5 cm is cut out from a circular cardboard of radius 4.2 cm. Find the ratio of the area of semi  -  circular cardboard to the area of circular cardboard.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>3.5 cm &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;&#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2337;&#2348;&#2379;&#2352;&#2381;&#2337; &#2325;&#2379; 4.2 cm &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2337;&#2348;&#2379;&#2352;&#2381;&#2337; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366;&#2335;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;-&#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2337;&#2348;&#2379;&#2352;&#2381;&#2337; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2337;&#2348;&#2379;&#2352;&#2381;&#2337; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">16:25</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">16:25</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">9:16</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">9:16</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">25:72</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">25:72</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">36:49</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">36:49</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Radius of semi - circular cardboard = 3.5 cm</p><p>Radius of circular cardboard = 4.2 cm</p><p>Area of semi - circular cardboard/area of circular cardboard = 1/2 * &#960; * 3.5 * 3.5/&#960; * 4.2 * 4.2 = 25/(36 * 2)</p><p>Required ratio = 25: 72</p>","marks":2,"section":null}]}